messages:
elaine: Heads-up — I'm doing a small tidy of the realtime quickstart (websocket example). Current snippet uses the old `sdk.connect()` and trips token refresh in our private deploys. Opening a draft PR: https://github.com/redwood/docs/pull/4321 — want to swap to the StreamingClient pattern and add an explicit reconnect + token-refresh note.

mike: Ack. Can you drop the PR link in the checklist? I'll review the code paths for reconnect/backoff. Quick Q: do we want the new example to show both browser + node usage or just node?

elaine: Prefer both but keep browser minimal. Browser example should be a single fetch-to-upgrade pattern then show `stream.on('message', ...)`. Node gets the fuller example with `await client.subscribe()` and small snippet for handling `401` on send.

samira: Also add a line about CORS preflight for websocket handshakes on private deployments — had a support ticket last week where customers missed the ALB config. Short sentence under troubleshooting should suffice.

ben (eng): I skimmed the draft. Two small nits: (1) change `maxRetries: 5` to `maxRetries: 3` in the sample (we prefer faster failover to fallback endpoints), (2) show `await client.close()` in the finally block so users don't leak sockets.

elaine: good catches. I'll update. Also plan to include a small code snippet for token refresh handling so the example doesn't look like a black box. Will it be OK to show a tiny helper?

mike: yep, lightweight helper is fine. Keep token logic fake (no real secrets). Example: ```js
// naive token refresher (demo only)
async function ensureToken(client) {
  if (client.tokenExpired()) {
    const newToken = await fetch('/_refresh_token').then(r=>r.text());
    client.setToken(newToken);
  }
}
```

samira: Suggest also a one-liner on how to turn on verbose logging for the streaming client so users can triage: `client.setLogLevel('debug')`.

elaine: adding that. Anything else? I'm going to squash a couple of tiny commits and request review from @mike and @ben.

docs-bot: CI started for PR #4321 — https://ci.redwood.internal/4321 — smoke tests: docs-build, linkchecker, sample-tests.

mike: I'll review after lunch. If we land this, could someone add a redirect from `/quickstart/realtime` -> `/quickstart/realtime-v2` in the nav? Quick win to avoid stale bookmarks.

elaine: yes will open a small docs nav PR after merge. Thanks all :thumbsup:

ben (eng): thanks — when you push updates ping me, I'll run the playback tests against dedicated infra to validate reconnect behavior.

elaine: will do. PR updated with the token helper + backoff tweaks, requesting reviews now.
